                <pb facs="0567" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg557"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 28.</seg></opener>
                <head>The Duke of Newcastle to Lieutenant Governor Gordon.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Downing Street</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 12, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that, by
                    papers which have reached me from Major General Doyle, it appears that the judge
                    of the vice-admiralty court at Hal fax has decreed the restoration of the
                    Chesapeake and her cargo to the owners.</p>
                <p>I am happy to take this opportunity of acquainting you that the whole of the
                    proceedings which you had occasion to adopt in connexion with this difficult
                    case have met with the entire approval of her Majesty’s government. I have,
                    &amp;c.,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">NEWCASTLE.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
